he exchange behind Poland, and 1:27 behind Sweden. On the second leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/81213"} "Mariya Gusakova"] " went away from Finland, but could only take 27 seconds on Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/82473"} "Britt Strandberg"] ". At the last exchange, " [:a {:href "/athletes/81003"} "Sonja Ruthström"] " of Sweden had a one minute lead on Soviet’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/80591"} "Lyubov Baranova"] ", and even though Baranova produced the fastest leg of the day, Ruthström easily secured the gold for Sweden, definitely one of the most unexpected cross country skiing victories in the Olympic history. In the individual 10 km event, the ladies on the Soviet team placed 1-2-3 and the Swedes 5-8-10! Finland’s skiers over the last two legs had no problems overtaking the Polish team to win the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Exchange"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1-04:21.4"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Lead-Off"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1-1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81412"} "Irma Johansson"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "21:31.0"] [:td {} "21:31.0 (1)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2nd Leg"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1-2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82473"} "Britt Strandberg"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "21:45.0"] [:td {} "43:16.0 (1)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Anchor"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1-3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81003"} "Sonja Ruthström"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "21:05.4"] [:td {} "1-0